```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <signal.h>
#include <unistd.h>

int main() {
    pid_t pid = fork();
    if (pid < 0) {
        perror("fork");
        return 1;
    }
    if (pid > 0) {
        // Parent process
        sleep(1);
        return 0;
    }
    // Child process
    sleep(2);
    kill(getppid(), SIGSEGV);
    return 0;
}
```
This program creates a new process using the `fork` system call. The parent process sleeps for 1 second, and the child process sleeps for 2 seconds. The child process then sends a SIGSEGV signal to the parent process using the `kill` system call.

